WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.350
One of the hardest things to get right is
how to make a great super-villain, and it

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.940
seems like filmmakers are just starting to
get the hang of it.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:11.340
There's a mind-blowing roster of classic comic
book baddies who are going to be hitting theaters

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.840
over the next couple of years.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.100
Skrulls are a nasty species of shapeshifting
aliens that have existed since the early days

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.140
of Marvel comics.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.700
In Captain Marvel, the most notable one will
be Talos, played by Ben Mendelsohn.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:28.260
In the comics, Talos is a relatively obscure
character, albeit a vicious warrior.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.920
He's certainly an unexpected choice for our
first major Skrull character in the MCU.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.920
His quality as a movie villain remains to
be seen, but a word of caution for viewers

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.000
of Captain Marvel: whenever you're dealing
with Skrulls, things are never what they seem.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.040
“Who else?

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:44.280
Who else is a Skrull and where are they?”

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:46.980
“We are everywhere.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:48.640
You will see.”

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:52.620
He may have died in the first Guardians of
the Galaxy film, but Ronan the Accuser, the

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.580
fanatical Kree warlord, will play a role in
the upcoming Captain Marvel.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:01.079
Not only is it generally great to see Lee
Pace return, it also makes a lot sense for

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:01.960
him to be here.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.340
Captain Marvel is a prequel, and the Kree
are heavily featured in Carol Danvers' origin.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.180
Yet Ronan might not end up being an antagonist
at all.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:13.260
Throughout the comics, Ronan is devoted to
doing what he feels is in the best interest

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:13.960
of the Kree.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:18.660
Sometimes he's trying to eliminate Earth’s
pesky superheroes, but sometimes he's teaming

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:19.420
up with them.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.520
Basically, he's a total wild card.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.000
“Tis the tinder on which you burn!”

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.299
Since the first trailer, fans have been tentatively
optimistic about Mark Strong's casting as

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.660
a beefier-than-usual Doctor Sivana in the
upcoming Shazam.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.150
To the uninitiated, Doctor Sivana might seem
like a checklist of the most generic villain

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:45.500
qualities throughout all of fiction were somehow
given human form, mainly due to appearing

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.140
way back in 1939.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.760
He's an evil bald doctor, and his actual catchphrase
is, "Curses!"

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.100
The movie Sivana appears to resemble the recent
New 52 design, where he’s more of a three-dimensional

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.080
human being than a cackling madman.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.320
Although it would be really fun if Mark Strong
went full maniacal villain, odds are good

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:05.800
that he's going to be playing Sivana pretty
straight.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.700
“No one can stop me this time!

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:12.640
Not even the world’s mightiest mortal, Captain
Marvel!”

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:17.680
Without question, one of the scariest villains
in superheroic history is Jean Grey's alter-ego,

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:18.420
Dark Phoenix.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:22.840
Unfortunately, we haven't had a screen adaptation
yet that has fully delivered on the potential

00:02:22.859 --> 00:02:23.859
of that character.

00:02:23.859 --> 00:02:28.270
In the comics, Jean bonds with an alien entity
known as the Phoenix Force while on a mission

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:31.620
in space, which in time becomes malevolent
and genocidal.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:36.230
Eventually an entire army of aliens shows
up to put Dark Phoenix down, and despite the

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:40.740
X-Men's attempts to save her, she dies in
a spectacular final battle on the moon.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:45.080
The movies are taking another shot at this
iconic story with this summer's Dark Phoenix.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.800
Will the character be able to rise from the
ashes of her previous incarnations?

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:53.900
Depends on which version of the X-Men franchise
shows up this summer — the good personality

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:54.860
or the evil one.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.380
“All is revealed.”

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:08.420
Dark Phoenix herself isn't the only potentially
epic X-Men baddie coming to the screen this

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:08.920
summer.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:13.300
Perhaps even more intriguing is a supporting
role that, at this stage, we know far less

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:13.840
about.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.640
Jessica Chastain is going to appear in Dark
Phoenix as… someone.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:22.339
According to director Simon Kinberg, she is
playing a new character partially inspired

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.260
by the Mastermind.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:28.400
The Mastermind is an old C-List Marvel character
with mind control powers who, in the comics,

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.000
was partially responsible for Phoenix turning
bad.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:35.359
This version of the character seems like it's
going to be very different from the mustachioed

00:03:35.359 --> 00:03:39.689
creep of the comics, not only because this
version is a woman, but also because she's

00:03:39.689 --> 00:03:41.260
apparently going to be an alien.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.819
The filmmakers have been cagey about revealing
much else, but there's still an entire universe

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:48.640
of possibilities for what could be going on
with this character.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:53.020
“You can’t begin to comprehend what you
are.”

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.620
Played by Milla Jovovich, Nimue the Blood
Queen is the Hellboy-verse's incarnation of

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:58.540
the Lady of the Lake.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:03.020
Once a human protege of Merlin, her lust for
power led her to betray Merlin.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:08.449
Nimue later discovered the Ogdru Jahad, interdimensional
space gods that empowered her to become the

00:04:08.449 --> 00:04:12.839
strongest magic user in the world and a conduit
through which they might someday be able to

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:13.400
enter it.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.400
Also, she can turn into a dragon.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.000
That's cool.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:21.220
We'll see how much of this ends up on screen,
but the trailer shows Hellboy wielding Excalibur,

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:24.870
and the promise of our favorite demon boy
using a magic sword to fight a space dragon

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.280
witch is certainly enough to get us excited.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:31.360
“Hellboy, your fall shall be like the fall
of mountains.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:33.360
I was before mountains.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:36.460
I was in the beginning and I shall be forever.”

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:42.539
The typically cuddly Ewan McGregor has been
cast as the Batman villain Roman Sionis, a.k.a.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.500
Black Mask, in the Birds of Prey film.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:49.260
From what we can see in the brief teaser trailer,
however, he is suspiciously maskless.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:53.900
In the comics, Sionis was a childhood friend
of Bruce Wayne, who started desperately committing

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.480
crimes while wearing a black mask.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:59.940
Bruce tried to get him to reform, but his
fate was sealed when a flaming building collapsed

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.940
on him, and his mask permanently fused into
his face.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.320
From then on, he was an irredeemable criminal.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:10.080
Based on what we've seen from preliminary
plot synopses, it's looking more likely that

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.600
Sionis is going to be all bad from the beginning,
and that's also exciting.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:18.700
Current day Black Mask is not only terrifyingly
cruel, but he also has a magic mask that hypnotizes

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.700
anyone who looks directly at it.

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:25.460
Considering Harley Quinn fought against black
magic in Suicide Squad, it’s totally plausible

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:29.669
that this version of Black Mask might not
just be a ruthless crime boss, but also a

00:05:29.669 --> 00:05:30.900
master of mentalism.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.400
“Don’t be nervous, kid.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:36.340
But keep staring at me like that and I’ll
cut your eyes out.”

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:44.160
The trailer for Spider-Man: Far From Home
introduced us to Jake Gyllenhaal playing a

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.960
character who is long overdue for a big screen
debut: Mysterio.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:52.660
Mysterio's main gimmick is that he commits
crimes with the help of illusions, often holographic

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:53.380
projections.

00:05:53.669 --> 00:05:57.900
At first glance, Gyllenhaal's portrayal looks
like it might be a radical reinterpretation

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:02.129
of the character in the sense that he’s
acting like a mystic superhero, but as is

00:06:02.129 --> 00:06:05.740
often the case with ol' Fishbowl, there is
probably some deception afoot.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:10.540
In his first comic appearance, he frames Spider-Man
for a string of robberies, and then presents

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:14.060
himself as a new superhero who will bring
Spider-Man to justice.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:18.800
“And now I will crush you once and for all!

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:22.480
HAHAHAHA!”

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:28.180
Wonder Woman 1984 will feature Kristen Wiig
as Cheetah, one of Wonder Woman's longest-running

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:29.500
and most compelling foes.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:33.740
Barbara Minerva was a knowledge-hungry archaeologist
who befriended Diana Prince.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:38.740
Minerva's obsession with ancient secrets led
her to tracking down an evil plant deity named

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:39.580
Urzkartaga.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:44.580
The deity cursed her by transforming her into
a half-cheetah monster with a taste for human

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:45.080
flesh.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:49.300
Minerva blamed Diana for not saving her as
she promised, and the two have been enemies

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.080
ever since.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:55.060
If properly executed, this has the potential
to be a truly heartbreaking story and our

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.400
hopes are officially up.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:58.380
“Blaming me changes nothing.”

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.060
“Don’t deny you cursed me, Diana.”

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:04.580
“You brought it on yourself.”

